A||||2||Raydar||How About An Ice Storm?||||1||
Z||000000||Raydar||01-29-2000||12:17 PM||||Okay. It's days like this that working for the power company becomes *interesting*. Had to drive 30 miles to work, at 6 AM. The last 7-8 miles were a sheet of ice. (No, I don't climb poles. I just support the computers in the emergency centers.) Had a 7th floor view of all the unfortunates (or crazies) on the hill in front of our building. Glad I wasn't out there. <BR>I'd *much prefer* a blizzard to this mess. At least snow doesn't bring down trees and power lines.  ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spyder||01-29-2000||12:32 PM||||Raydar<BR>I live 3 hours south of Atlanta in Albany GA. They had predicted the ice storm for us, but we were very fortunate to just get rain and above freezing temperature. Thank goodness, I would hate to see the idiots around here on ice.   I only remember it snowing here once, twenty four years ago.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Wolfhound||01-29-2000||01:45 PM||||I,m near Auburn Ala just off Hy. 85 and we had just enough snow to cover the tops of cars earley friday morning (maybe an inch). It was melted by 10:00 AM and and has been raining off and on since. No Ice luckily.||||reg||1
